{"repositoryId":798445858,"availability":"available","full":"chromascope-ms/chromascope","name":"chromascope","description":"Open-source, AI-ready LC–MS workbench built in Rust. Interactive visualization, peak integration, batch quantification, and MCP-powered automation.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Rust","stars":17,"forks":1,"created":"2024-05-09T19:44:51Z","updated":"2026-10-19T16:07:07Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://chromascope-ms.github.io/chromascope/","topics":["chromatography","gui-application","mass-spectrometry","science-research","scientific-visualization"],"demo":"https://chromascope-ms.github.io/chromascope/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:11.165Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:11.165Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:11.165Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T07:12:57.832Z","stars":17,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-19T18:05:11.165Z","stars":17,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AI-assisted LC-MS analysis, across instrument vendors, with traceable results.","Chromascope is a free, open-source LC-MS workbench written in Rust. Open mzML data, draw chromatograms and spectra, integrate peaks, build calibration curves, quantify and run QC. Use it like a normal desktop app, script it from the command line, or hand the controls to an AI assistant over MCP. The assistant does the reasoning; Chromascope does the maths, keeps the evidence and records exactly what happened.","Video not playing? Open assets/demo.mp4 directly. It shows an AI client opening a file, extracting an XIC and previewing an integration in the Chromascope window; nothing is changed permanently."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chromascope-ms/chromascope/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ab222f1f491e6d941d49633cb553db1e169f93bc81bece3496c5484b322f49ec","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:11.293Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:11.293Z","